This skill draws on two MIT-licensed sources. The text is rewritten; the ideas are theirs.

- `full-send` and `full-stop` in tstack (https://github.com/t3dotgg/tstack): the two endings, a spoken
  grant of autonomy, proof as evidence observed in the session, and a written merge gate.
- The shipping, babysit, opening-a-pr and autopilot playbooks and the `blast-radius` skill in pstack
  (https://github.com/cursor/plugins, folder `pstack`): a verdict belongs to a commit, the independent
  check, the order of work on a pull request, classifying a failing check, and the proof ladder.

